Finally my mother asks about the winter.
The weather changed suddenly.
It was windy, and the air was ice cold.
The cold bit my cheeks on the way to work.
I needed some warm clothes.
After work, I hurried into a large store.
Fortunately, it was wonderfully warm inside.
A young man was working in the store.
He came over to me and smiled.
He asked, "Are you looking for something specific?"
I answered, "Yes please, I would like to buy your warmest winter jacket."
He found a thick, dark blue jacket for me.
I tried it on immediately.
It was wonderfully warm, and it fit perfectly.
I also found a pair of good winter boots.
I took the things up to the register and paid.
The clothes cost one thousand kroner.
It was a bit expensive, but it was absolutely necessary.
My mother smiled through the screen.
She was glad that I was finally warm.
